        description: '<strong>Cumulative QA failure log.</strong> Every failing QA verdict — spec gates, the per-PRD feature loop, the plan QA note, the <code>verify.sh</code> build/test gate, and the implementation judgment gate — is appended in full to <code>.gspec/build/qa-failures.md</code>, tagged with the stage, checker, target, and whether it was a self-heal revision (<code>rev N</code>), a downgraded advisory (<code>ADVISORY</code>), or the <code>TERMINAL</code> failure that paused the run. Recovered failures are captured too, so a build that self-heals and completes still leaves a reviewable record. Previously a recovered failure left only a truncated manifest excerpt, and the one detailed report (<code>last-failure.md</code>) was overwritten by the next failure and deleted on completion. The new log is cumulative across runs and never auto-removed — delete it once you have mined it; the end-of-run learnings report and the paused-build banner both point at it.',
